SUPER-EARTH, PROXIMA B -- super-earth-proxima-b.jpg -- 2048 x 1024
Credit: NASA Visualization Technology Applications and Development (VTAD).
Official source: https://science.nasa.gov/resource/proxima-b-3d-model/
Model released 1 May 2019; download published 20 September 2023.
Download: https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/astro/exo-explore/2023/09/Proxima_b_1_13776.glb
Downloaded GLB SHA-256: d534dc69c165754da0cd49b69425e77565e79d5a53c3c4b3bbc582b77518ae7a
Selected embedded base-colour image: image 0, exo_PROXIMA_CEN_B.jpg (stored as PNG).
Processing: extracted the original 2048 x 1024 equirectangular PNG from the GLB
image buffer view and encoded it as RGB JPEG (Pillow, quality 95, subsampling 0).
No resizing, cropping, terrain generation or colour adjustment. The separate
metallic/roughness image is unused. No generative AI is used.
This is an artist's concept, not a photograph or an observed surface map.
Land, water and clouds are speculative; the image does not establish habitability.
The source identifies Proxima b as a super-Earth. Selecting it does not set a
planetary mass or radius; Image radius / outer remains the user's setting.
